{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01685Y3vP57WDZxLex7kuh8F","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-14-0730-overlap-logup-precompute-round0\n2\t\n3\tOverlap the logup combination precomputation (d_eq_3b upload + precompute_logup_combinations kernel launches) with Round 0 multi-stream evaluation by running it on a background thread with its own CUDA stream. Currently, 1582 per-trace precompute kernel launches (37ms GPU time) plus ~791 H2D uploads (~5-8ms) run sequentially on the default stream BEFORE Round 0 starts, even though their output is only consumed later during MLE rounds. Round 0 uses only host-side eq_3b values for weight computation, so the device-side precompute is entirely independent. By spawning the precompute on a background thread concurrent with Round 0 (which runs ~55ms of multi-stream evaluation per segment at ~42% GPU utilization), the ~22ms per-segment precompute work is fully hidden, saving ~44ms total across two segments.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d4314f39-e91d-47fe-87bd-a8908ed81e1e","uuid":"35f1029e-cc2c-4207-8bfe-fc90aaf616ec","timestamp":"2026-04-14T05:47:43.399Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-14-0730-overlap-logup-precompute-round0\n\nOverlap the logup combination precomputation (d_eq_3b upload + precompute_logup_combinations kernel launches) with Round 0 multi-stream evaluation by running it on a background thread with its own CUDA stream. Currently, 1582 per-trace precompute kernel launches (37ms GPU time) plus ~791 H2D uploads (~5-8ms) run sequentially on the default stream BEFORE Round 0 starts, even though their output is only consumed later during MLE rounds. Round 0 uses only host-side eq_3b values for weight computation, so the device-side precompute is entirely independent. By spawning the precompute on a background thread concurrent with Round 0 (which runs ~55ms of multi-stream evaluation per segment at ~42% GPU utilization), the ~22ms per-segment precompute work is fully hidden, saving ~44ms total across two segments.\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
