don2Digest;\n\n    unsafe fn compress_rows(\n        out: &mut DeviceBuffer<Self::Digest>,\n        matrix: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n        width: usize,\n        query_stride: usize,\n        log_rows_per_query: usize,\n    ) -> Result<(), CudaError> {\n        poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes(out, matrix, width, query_stride, log_rows_per_query)\n    }\n    \n    unsafe fn compress_layer(...) -> Result<(), CudaError> {\n        poseidon2_adjacent_compress_layer(output, prev_layer, output_size)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. DATA FLOW SUMMARY\n\n```\nProvingContext<PB>\n  │\n  ├─ per_trace: Vec<(usize, AirProvingContext<PB>)>\n  │  └─ AirProvingContext\n  │     └─ common_main: DeviceMatrix<F>  [Device-side trace matrices]\n  │\n  ▼ [sorted by descending height for stacking]\n  \nCoordinator::prove() calls self.device.commit(&traces)\n  │\n  ▼\nGpuDevice::commit()\n  │\n  ▼\nstacked_commit() [stacked_pcs.rs:48-84]\n  │\n  ├─ [Stack traces via batched scatter kernel]\n  │  ├─ Input: Multiple DeviceMatrix<F>\n  │  ├─ Process: Build StackColDesc array, upload, launch stack_columns_kernel\n  │  ├─ Kernel: matrix.cu lines 232-243\n  │  └─ Output: Single stacked DeviceMatrix<F> [column-major]\n  │\n  ├─ [RS code via MLE interpolation + NTT]\n  │  ├─ batch_expand_pad: Evaluate on coset\n  │  ├─ batch_ntt: Forward NTT\n  │  └─ Output: Reed-Solomon codeword matrix\n  │\n  ├─ [Merkle tree construction]\n  │  ├─ Input: RS codeword matrix [width×height, column-major]\n  │  │\n  │  ├─ compress_rows() ← 231ms GPU time\n  │  │  └─ poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel\n  │  │     ├─ For each query_stride index: hash 2^log_rows_per_query strided rows\n  │  │     ├─ Row hash: sponge over [width] column values\n  │  │     ├─ Merkle tree: log_rows_per_query layers of hashing pairs\n  │  │     └─ Output: query_stride root hashes\n  │  │\n  │  └─ compress_layer() × log_depth times\n  │     └─ poseidon2_strided_compress_layer_kernel\n  │        ├─ Compress adjacent digest pairs\n  │        ├─ Output size = input size / 2\n  │        └─ Repeat until 1 root remains\n  │\n  └─ Output: MerkleTreeGpu<F, Digest>\n     └─ struct fields:\n        ├─ digest_layers: Vec<DeviceBuffer<Digest>>  [all layers]\n        ├─ root: Digest                             [root only on host]\n        └─ backing_matrix: Option<DeviceMatrix<F>>  [cached for openings]\n\nReturn: (root_commitment, StackedPcsDataGpu)\n  │\n  ▼ [Flow to constraint proving]\n  \nCoordinator::prove() continues with:\n  └─ transcript.observe_commit(common_main_commit)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 8. HASH PARAMETERS & CONSTANTS\n\n**Poseidon2 Configuration:**\n- **CELLS_RATE:** Absorption rate per permutation (defined in poseidon2.cuh)\n- **CELLS_OUT:** Output size of Poseidon2 permutation (8 BabyBear Fp elements = 256 bits)\n- **Permutation:** WIDTH=3, 4 external + 56 internal + 4 external rounds = 64 total\n\n**Sponge Constants (BN254 variant in bn254_poseidon2.cu):**\n- BN254_BABY_BEAR_RATE = 16 (BabyBear values per permutation)\n- BN254_NUM_F_ELMS = 8 (BabyBear values packed per Bn254Fr)\n\n**Memory Layout:**\n- Column-major matrix: element at (col, row) stored at `col * height + row`\n- Shared memory per block: `CELLS_OUT * blockDim.x * (blockDim.y / 2)` Fp elements\n\n---\n\n### 9. POTENTIAL OPTIMIZATIONS & OBSERVATIONS\n\n**Current Bottleneck (231ms):**\n- Row hashing dominates due to full column reads per trace\n- Each thread-block processes ONE query\n- Memory access pattern: column-major with sequential row reads (coalesced)\n\n**Redundant Computations Analysis:**\n1. **Row Hash Redundancy:** If same trace appears in multiple AIRs, row hashes computed separately\n   - Current: No caching layer between traces\n   - Mitigation: Some pre-computation via cached_mains in AirProvingContext\n   \n2. **Merkle Compression:** Adjacent layer compression is straightforward (no redundancy)\n\n3. **Stack_columns Batching:** Recent optimization (commit `79314f3c`) already batches scatter via descriptor arrays\n\n**O