{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011v9zeRP9atQsxXWAYtC9qw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-14-0830-increase-gkr-input-streams-roundrobin\n2\t\n3\tIncrease the GKR input evaluation thread count from 8 to 16 and switch from contiguous chunk distribution to round-robin (interleaved) work assignment. The GKR input eval for seg0 at APC 300 takes ~242ms with 8 threads using contiguous chunking on height-sorted work items, giving thread 0 all the largest AIRs (worst-case load balance). With pre-allocated per-thread buffers already eliminating mutex contention (since the prealloc-gkr-input-buffers task), higher thread counts are now viable without the allocation serialization that previously limited scaling. The combination of more threads (finer work granularity) and round-robin distribution (each thread gets a mix of large and small AIRs) should improve GPU stream overlap and reduce the critical-path thread time.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01TTJtCvnA6KHWz7rCbysKna","session_id":"d4314f39-e91d-47fe-87bd-a8908ed81e1e","uuid":"de221969-12c4-469e-9893-236cf5b07ab6","timestamp":"2026-04-14T09:02:21.953Z"}
