const Rule *d_rules,\n    const size_t *d_used_nodes,\n    const uint32_t *d_pair_idxs,\n    size_t used_nodes_len,\n    uint32_t permutation_height,\n    uint32_t num_rows_per_tile\n)\n```\n\n**Grid/Block Computation (Lines 231-232):**\n```cuda\nauto count = is_global ? TASK_SIZE : permutation_height;  // TASK_SIZE = (1 << 16) = 65536\nauto [grid, block] = kernel_launch_params(count, 256);\n```\n\n**kernel_launch_params Formula** (from `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/include/launcher.cuh` lines 14-21):\n```cuda\ninline std::pair<dim3, dim3> kernel_launch_params(size_t count, size_t threads_per_block = MAX_THREADS) {\n    size_t block = std::min(count, threads_per_block);  // block.x = min(count, 256)\n    size_t grid = div_ceil(count, block);               // grid.x = ceil(count / block.x)\n    return std::make_pair(dim3(grid, 1, 1), dim3(block, 1, 1));\n}\n```\n\n**Mode Selection (Lines 233-263):**\n- **GLOBAL mode (true):** Uses `TASK_SIZE = 65536` threads, distributes work across task_stride with global intermediates buffer\n- **SCATTER mode (false):** Uses `permutation_height` threads, each thread keeps local 10-element intermediates array (line 89)\n\n---\n\n### 3. RUST FFI BINDING\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` (Lines 278-292)\n\n**C FFI Declaration:**\n```rust\nfn _logup_gkr_input_eval(\n    is_global: bool,\n    fracs: *mut Frac<EF>,\n    preprocessed: *const F,\n    partitioned_main: *const u64,\n    public_values: *const F,\n    challenges: *const EF,\n    intermediates: *const EF,\n    rules: *const std::ffi::c_void,\n    used_nodes: *const usize,\n    pair_idxs: *const u32,\n    used_nodes_len: usize,\n    height: u32,\n    num_rows_per_tile: u32,\n) -> i32;\n```\n\n**Rust Wrapper Function** (Lines 938-968):\n```rust\npub unsafe fn logup_gkr_input_eval(\n    is_global: bool,\n    fracs: *mut Frac<EF>,\n    preprocessed: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    partitioned_main: &DeviceBuffer<u64>,\n    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    challenges: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    intermediates: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    rules: &DeviceBuffer<u128>,\n    used_nodes: &DeviceBuffer<usize>,\n    pair_idxs: &DeviceBuffer<u32>,\n    height: u32,\n    num_rows_per_tile: u32,\n) -> Result<(), CudaError>\n```\n\n**Dispatcher Pattern:**\n- Single function handles both GLOBAL and SCATTER modes through `is_global` boolean flag\n- All data passed as device pointers (rules, used_nodes, pair_idxs are per-AIR, not batched)\n- **Currently: No batching support** — called once per AIR (seen in gkr_input.rs line 174)\n\n---\n\n### 4. DATA STRUCTURES & DAG EVALUATION\n\n**Source Encoding Structure** (from `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/include/codec.cuh` lines 33-38):\n\n```cuda\ntypedef struct {\n    EntryType type;  // ENTRY_PREPROCESSED, ENTRY_MAIN, SRC_INTERMEDIATE, etc.\n    uint8_t part;    // partition index for ENTRY_MAIN\n    uint8_t offset;  // row offset (rotation)\n    uint32_t index;  // column or constant value\n} SourceInfo;\n```\n\n**Rule Encoding** (Lines 12-15, 40-47):\n```cuda\ntypedef struct {\n    uint64_t low;   // Contains x source (48 bits) encoded\n    uint64_t high;  // Contains y source, z_index, op, buffer_result, is_constraint\n} Rule;\n\n// Lazy decoded header (reduces register pressure):\ntypedef struct {\n    bool is_constraint;\n    bool buffer_result;\n    OperationType op;   // ADD, SUB, MUL, NEG, VAR\n    SourceInfo x;\n} RuleHeader;\n```\n\n**DAG Evaluation Helper** (Lines 17-63):\n\n```cuda\n__device__ __forceinline__ FpExt evaluate_dag_entry_gkr(\n    const SourceInfo &src,\n    uint32_t row_index,\n    const Fp *d_preprocessed,\n    const uint64_t *d_main,          // Array of pointers to partitions\n    const Fp *d_public_values,\n    const FpExt *d_challenges,\n    const FpExt *d_intermediates,\n    const uint32_t intermediate_stride,\n    const uint32_t height\n)\n```\n\n**Evaluation Strategy:**\n- Switch on `src.type` to load from:\n  - Preprocessed trace: `d_preprocessed[height * src.index + ((row + src.offset) % height)]`\n  - Main trace partition: `d_main[src.part]` cast to `Fp*`, then indexed similarly\n  - Public values: `d_public_values[src.index]`\n  - Challenges: `d_challenges[src.index]` (FpExt, global per protocol)\n  - Intermediates: `d_intermediates[intermediate_stride * src.index]` (per-row DAG cache)\n  - Constants/IS_FIRST/IS_LAST/IS_TRANSITION: Computed inline\n\n**Per-AIR vs Shared Data:**\n- **Per-AIR (descriptor needed):** `d_rules`, `d_used_nodes`, `d_pair_idxs`, `permutation_height`, `buffer_size`, `d_intermediates` allocation size\n- **Shared (global):** `d_preprocessed`, `d_main` (partitions), `d_public_values`, `d_challenges` (same challenges across all AIRs in proof)\n\n---\n\n### 5. INTERACTION EVALUATION FLOW\n\n**Lines 98-205 (Main loop):**\n\n1. **Row loop** (lines 94-207): Each thread processes `num_rows_per_tile` rows\n2. **Used nodes iteration** (lines 100-205): Loop over `used_nodes_len` entries\n   - `d_used_nodes[used_idx]` maps to rule index to evaluate\n   - Pattern: alternates numerator/denominator constraint evaluation\n3. **Lazy DAG construction** (lines 103-121, 123-198):\n   - If `node_idx < rules_evaluated`: Reuse cached intermediate (line 120)\n   - Else: Evaluate all rules from `rules_evaluated` up to `node_idx` (lines 123-198)\n   - Store buffered results via `decode_z_index(rule)` at `intermediates_ptr[z_index * intermediate_stride]`\n4. **Output mapping** (lines 201-204):\n   - `pair_idx = d_pair_idxs[used_idx]` — maps used_idx to (interaction_idx, is_denom)\n   - Output written to: `d_fracs[(interaction_idx * height + row) * 2 + (pair_idx & 1)]`\n   - This layout: **[interaction_idx][row][numer/denom]**\n\n---\n\n### 6. INTERMEDIATES BUFFER STRATEGY\n\n**GLOBAL Mode (Lines 85-87):**\n- Pointer: `intermediates_ptr = (FpExt *)d_intermediates + task_offset`\n- Stride: `intermediate_stride = task_stride` (distance between same thread's rows)\n- Layout: `[buffer_size][num_threads][num_rows_per_tile]`\n- Size: `buffer_size * TASK_SIZE * 1 = buffer_size * 65536` FpExt elements when fully used\n- Decision: `is_global = buffer_size > 10` (see gkr_input.rs line 160)\n\n**SCATTER Mode (Lines 88-92):**\n- Local array: `FpExt intermediates[10]` (max 10 cached intermediate nodes)\n- Stride: `intermediate_stride = 1` (contiguous in local array)\n- Max buffer_size: 10 (hardcoded)\n- Constraint: No global intermediates buffer; fast path for small DAGs\n\n---\n\n### 7. EXISTING BATCHED KERNEL PATTERNS\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle.cu` (Lines 109-204)\n\n**Batched Kernel Example (zerocheck_batch_mle_kernel):**\n\n```cuda\n__global__ void zerocheck_batch_mle_kernel(\n    FpExt *__restrict__ tmp_sums_buffer,\n    const BlockCtx *__restrict__ d_block_ctxs,      // Descriptor array\n    const ZerocheckCtx *__restrict__ d_zc_ctxs,     // Per-AIR contexts\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_lambda_pows,\n    size_t lambda_len\n)\n```\n\n**Batching Pattern (Lines 119-125):**\n```cuda\nBlockCtx block_ctx = d_block_ctxs[blockIdx.x];\nZerocheckCtx zc_ctx = d_zc_ctxs[block_ctx.air_idx];  // Load per-AIR descriptor\n\nuint32_t num_x = gridDim.y;\nuint32_t x_int = blockIdx.y;\nuint32_t y_int = threadIdx.x + block_ctx.local_block_idx_x * blockDim.x;\n```\n\n**BlockCtx Definition** (from `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` lines 17-22):\n```rust\n#[repr(C)]\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\npub struct BlockCtx {\n    pub local_block_idx_x: u32,\n    /// Refers to index within buffer of `ZerocheckCtx` or `LogupCtx`\n    pub air_idx: u32,\n}\n```\n\n**Per-AIR Context Structure (ZerocheckCtx)** (Lines 15-25 of batch_mle.cu):\n```cuda\nstruct ZerocheckCtx {\n    EvalCoreCtx eval_ctx;                          // shared pointers\n    FpExt *__restrict__ d_intermediates;           // per-AIR\n    uint32_t num_y;                                 // per-AIR\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_eq_xi;              // per-AIR\n    const Rule *__restrict__ d_rules;               // per-AIR\n    size_t rules_len;                               // per-AIR\n    const size_t *__restrict__ d_used_nodes;        // per-AIR\n    size_t used_nodes_len;                          // per-AIR\n    uint32_t buffer_size;                           // per-AIR\n};\n```\n\n**Key Insight:** Batched kernels use descriptor arrays where each block/warp loads `block_ctx[blockIdx.x]` to get its AIR index, then loads per-AIR state from `d_zc_ctxs[air_idx]`.\n\n---\n\n### 8. DESCRIPTOR STRUCT FOR BATCHED GKR VERSION\n\nBased on the existing patterns, here's what a **per-AIR descriptor for batched GKR input eval** would need:\n\n```cuda\nstruct GkrInputDesc {\n    // Shared evaluation context (same across all AIRs)\n    const Fp *d_preprocessed;\n    const uint64_t *d_main;                    // Array of partitions\n    const Fp *d_public_values;\n    const FpExt *d_challenges;\n    \n    // Per-AIR rule data\n    const Rule *d_rules;\n    const size_t *d_used_nodes;\n    const uint32_t *d_pair_idxs;\n    size_t used_nodes_len;\n    \n    // Per-AIR dimensions and buffers\n    uint32_t permutation_height;\n    uint32_t buffer_size;                      // Determines GLOBAL vs SCATTER\n    FpExt *d_intermediates;                    // NULL if SCATTER, allocated if GLOBAL\n    uint32_t intermediate_stride;              // stride for GLOBAL mode\n    \n    // Output buffer (could be in parent array or separate)\n    FracExt *d_fracs;                          // output: [num_interactions][height][2]\n};\n```\n\n**Size Estimate:**\n- Fixed overhead: 11 pointers + 4 uint32_t + 1 size_t = ~88 bytes (64-bit pointers)\n- Highly cache-friendly for descriptor array loading\n- Per-AIR intermediates buffer: `buffer_size * TASK_SIZE * sizeof(FpExt)` (only if GLOBAL mode)\n\n---\n\n### 9. CONTROL FLOW VARIANCE ACROSS AIRs\n\n**Kernel Control Flow is Per-AIR Variant:**\n\n1. **Intermediate buffer strategy decision:**\n   - If `buffer_size > 10`: Use GLOBAL mode with shared global buffer\n   - Else: Use SCATTER mode with local array\n   - **This varies per AIR** — needs per-AIR decision\n\n2. **DAG structure variance:**\n   - `d_rules`, `d_used_nodes`, `d_pair_idxs` are completely different per AIR\n   - Rule evaluation loop (lines 123-198) iterates per-AIR `rules_len`\n   - Output layout per AIR: `num_interactions` varies\n\n3. **Data dimensions:**\n   - `permutation_height` different per AIR\n   - Number of partitions (`d_main` structure) may differ\n\n**Critical for batching:** Cannot use warp-divergence-free template specialization; must handle GLOBAL/SCATTER decision per-block or use runtime branch with per-AIR descriptor.\n\n---\n\n### 10. PER-AIR STATE ACCESSED\n\n**State per thread throughout kernel execution:**\n\n1. **Registers/Local:**\n   - `task_offset`, `task_stride`, `row`, `rules_evaluated`, `used_idx`, `node_idx`\n   - `result` (FpExt), intermediate values `x`, `y`\n   - Local intermediates array (SCATTER mode only): `FpExt intermediates[10]` = 160 bytes\n\n2. **Global Memory (per-AIR descriptor):**\n   - `d_rules[node_idx]` — 128 bits per rule\n   - `d_used_nodes[used_idx]` — 64 bits per used node\n   - `d_pair_idxs[used_idx]` — 32 bits per pair mapping\n   - `d_intermediates[z_index * stride]` — 256 bits per intermediate (FpExt in Baby Bear)\n   - Evaluation sources: preprocessed, main, public, challenges\n\n3. **Working Set per Row:**\n   - Intermediates buffer for one row: `buffer_size * sizeof(FpExt)` (GLOBAL mode)\n   - With GLOBAL intermediates stride = task_stride, each thread row accesses its own slice\n\n**Estimation for batched kernel:**\n- Per-AIR descriptor: ~88 bytes\n- Per-thread local storage: ~160 bytes (SCATTER) or 0 (GLOBAL, use global buffer)\n- Per-row global intermediates: `buffer_size * 256 bits` (shared allocation pattern as in MLE kernel)\n\n---\n\n### 11. KEY FILES & LINE RANGES SUMMARY\n\n| Item | File | Lines |\n|------|------|-------|\n| Kernel definitions (GLOBAL & SCATTER) | `gkr_input.cu` | 65-208 |\n| Launcher function | `gkr_input.cu` | 216-265 |\n| Rust FFI | `logup_zerocheck.rs` | 278-292, 938-968 |\n| Data structures (Rule, SourceInfo) | `codec.cuh` | 12-48 |\n| DAG evaluation function | `gkr_input.cu` | 17-63 |\n| Config/launch params | `launcher.cuh` | 14-21 |\n| Batched MLE pattern reference | `batch_mle.cu` | 15-40, 109-204 |\n| BlockCtx/LogupCtx definitions | `logup_zerocheck.rs` | 17-75 |\n| gkr_input.rs usage pattern | `gkr_input.rs` | 112-210 |\n\n---\n\n### 12. RECOMMENDATIONS FOR BATCHED VERSION\n\n**Approach:** Adapt the `batch_mle_kernel` pattern\n\n1. **Descriptor Array Strategy:**\n   - Create `GkrInputDesc` array with all per-AIR data\n   - Each block reads `blockIdx.x` to select AIR\n   - Use 2D grid: `grid.x = num_air_blocks`, `grid.y = 1` (or fold into single dimension)\n\n2. **Handling GLOBAL vs SCATTER:**\n   - Per-AIR flag in descriptor: `use_global = buffer_size > 10`\n   - If batching always GLOBAL: pre-allocate combined intermediates buffer\n   - Runtime branch on `use_global` to decide pointer strategy\n\n3. **Work Distribution:**\n   - Keep row-tiling approach: `row = task_offset + j * task_stride`\n   - Each block handles one (AIR, row_tile) pair or all rows of one AIR\n   - Consider: different heights per AIR → pad with guard checks\n\n4. **Shared Memory:**\n   - Keep minimal (no cross-AIR synchronization needed)\n   - Per-AIR intermediates in global only (no shared cache)\n\n5. **Launch Configuration:**\n   - Kernel must be called once with all block_ctxs and desc arrays\n   - Grid size: `sum of (num_blocks_per_air)` across all AIRs\n   - Alternatively: single grid with descriptor-based load balancing\n\nThis design mirrors the batched MLE kernels successfully used in the same codebase, ensuring compatibility with the existing infrastructure."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d4314f39-e