{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YJTEHwhtRBJhexCQRzAsJV","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-14-0830-batch-scatter-gkr-input-eval\n2\t\n3\tBatch SCATTER-mode GKR input evaluation AIRs into a single descriptor-array CUDA kernel launch per segment, running on a dedicated background thread concurrent with the existing multi-stream GLOBAL-mode processing. At APC 300, ~305 of the 791 GKR input eval kernel instances use SCATTER mode (buffer_size <= 10), each launching a tiny kernel (median 111us, 4-16 blocks). These underutilize the GPU's 128 SMs when launched individually. By consolidating all SCATTER AIRs into one batched kernel (following the established `batch_mle` descriptor-array pattern), we eliminate ~305 kernel launches and their CPU-side overhead, while freeing the 8 multi-stream worker threads to focus exclusively on the ~486 compute-heavy GLOBAL-mode AIRs. The SCATTER batch runs concurrently on a separate thread, completely hidden behind the GLOBAL processing.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WVgYuHXQhJGV2tfoj6TCzi","session_id":"d4314f39-e91d-47fe-87bd-a8908ed81e1e","uuid":"483a3627-7794-4bf8-a1c9-b43af9bfe483","timestamp":"2026-04-14T09:15:34.452Z"}
