{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qqk3Tcs9s39hB2tupbJ7JA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Batch SCATTER-mode GKR Input Evaluation\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tReduce LogUp GKR input evaluation wall-clock time at APC 300 by batching SCATTER-mode AIR evaluations (buffer_size <= 10) into a single descriptor-array CUDA kernel per segment, launched on a dedicated background thread concurrent with the existing multi-stream GLOBAL-mode processing.\n6\t\n7\tLogUp GKR is 534ms (40.7% of STARK excl trace at APC 300). The GKR input eval sub-phase is ~302ms across 2 segments (~242ms seg0, ~62ms seg1). From nsight profiling: 486 GLOBAL-mode instances (464ms GPU time, median 760us) + 305 SCATTER-mode instances (63ms GPU time, median 111us). SCATTER AIRs each launch a tiny kernel with 4-16 blocks that underutilizes the 128 SMs.\n8\t\n9\t**Key mechanism**: Remove ~150 SCATTER AIRs per segment from the 8 multi-stream worker threads. Each thread processes ~20 GLOBAL-only AIRs instead of ~39 mixed AIRs. The SCATTER batch runs on a 9th background thread, hidden behind the GLOBAL processing. Each GLOBAL worker thread saves ~19 per-AIR overheads: CPU preparation (~25us), kernel launch (~10us), and between-kernel scheduling gap (~50us). Per-thread savings: ~1.6ms. The critical-path thread improves because its total serial work is shorter.\n10\t\n11\tAdditionally, the batched SCATTER kernel (one launch, ~1500 blocks) processes all SCATTER AIRs with optimal GPU block scheduling, vs the current approach where tiny 4-16 block kernels leave most SMs idle during each launch.\n12\t\n13\t## Current Code Path\n14\t\n15\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`\n16\t\n17\t1. **`log_gkr_input_evals()`** (line 215): Entry point.\n18\t   - Line 232-252: Build `Vec<GkrInputWorkItem>`, sort by descending height\n19\t   - Line 254-279: Compute max buffer sizes for pre-allocation\n20\t   - Line 282: Barrier sync\n21\t   - Line 285-289: Set num_threads (8 if >= 100 AIRs, else 1)\n22\t   - Line 291-303: Memory budget check (halve num_threads if pre-alloc > 2GB)\n23\t   - Line 306-321: Pre-allocate per-thread `GkrThreadBuffers`\n24\t   - Line 328-348: Multi-threaded processing: contiguous chunks, all AIR types mixed\n25\t\n26\t2. **`process_gkr_input_air()`** (line 112): Per-AIR processing.\n27\t   - Line 125-129: Build partition pointers from cached_mains + common_main\n28\t   - Line 141-148: Upload public_values to device via `copy_to`\n29\t   - Line 152-156: Upload partition_ptrs to device via `copy_to`\n30\t   - Line 158-160: `is_global = buffer_size > 10` — determines SCATTER vs GLOBAL mode\n31\t   - Line 173-187: Single FFI call: `logup_gkr_input_eval(is_global, ...)`\n32\t   - Line 189-208: Conditional lifting: if height != lifted_height, scale + repeat\n33\t\n34\t3. **CUDA kernel**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu`\n35\t   - Line 65-208: `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<GLOBAL>` template\n36\t   - SCATTER (GLOBAL=false, line 89-92): `FpExt intermediates[10]` — local array, max 10 nodes\n37\t   - GLOBAL (GLOBAL=true, line 85-87): `d_intermediates` global buffer, stride = task_stride\n38\t   - Line 17-63: `evaluate_dag_entry_gkr()` — switch on SourceInfo.type to load data\n39\t   - Line 94-207: Per-row loop: iterate d_used_nodes, evaluate DAG, write to d_fracs\n40\t   - Line 216-265: Launcher: `grid = kernel_launch_params(is_global ? TASK_SIZE : height, 256)`\n41\t\n42\t4. **FFI**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n43\t   - Line 278-292: extern declaration\n44\t   - Line 938-968: safe wrapper `logup_gkr_input_eval()`\n45\t\n46\t**Existing batched pattern reference**: `ZerocheckCtx` (line 48-58 of `cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`) + `BlockCtx` (line 17-22) used by `zerocheck_batch_mle_kernel` in `cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle.cu`. Each block reads `BlockCtx` to find its AIR, then loads the per-AIR `ZerocheckCtx` struct containing `d_rules`, `d_used_nodes`, `used_nodes_len`, `buffer_size`, etc.\n47\t\n48\t## Changes\n49\t\n50\t### Change 1: Define GkrInputScatterCtx descriptor struct\n51\t\n52\t**Files**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu` (CUDA) and `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` (Rust)\n53\t\n54\tCUDA side (add to gkr_input.cu, before the launcher function):\n55\t```cuda\n56\tstruct GkrInputScatterCtx {\n57\t    FracExt *d_fracs;               // Per-AIR output pointer (into leaves buffer)\n58\t    const Fp *d_preprocessed;       // Per-AIR preprocessed trace (or null)\n59\t    const uint64_t *d_main;         // Per-AIR partition pointers (device array)\n60\t    const Fp *d_public_values;      // Per-AIR public values (or null)\n61\t    const FpExt *d_challenges;      // Shared challenge vector (same for all AIRs)\n62\t    const Rule *d_rules;            // Per-AIR interaction DAG rules\n63\t    const size_t *d_used_nodes;     // Per-AIR used node indices\n64\t    const uint32_t *d_pair_idxs;    // Per-AIR pair index mapping\n65\t    size_t used_nodes_len;          // Per-AIR\n66\t    uint32_t permutation_height;    // Per-AIR trace height\n67\t    uint32_t num_blocks;            // Number of blocks assigned to this AIR\n68\t};\n69\t```\n70\t\n71\tRust side (add to `cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`, near existing context structs):\n72\t```rust\n73\t#[repr(C)]\n74\t#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\n75\tpub struct GkrInputScatterCtx {\n76\t    pub d_fracs: *mut Frac<EF>,\n77\t    pub d_preprocessed: *const F,\n78\t    pub d_main: *const u64,\n79\t    pub d_public_values: *const F,\n80\t    pub d_challenges: *const EF,\n81\t    pub d_rules: *const std::ffi::c_void,\n82\t    pub d_used_nodes: *const usize,\n83\t    pub d_pair_idxs: *const u32,\n84\t    pub used_nodes_len: usize,\n85\t    pub permutation_height: u32,\n86\t    pub num_blocks: u32,\n87\t}\n88\tunsafe impl Send for GkrInputScatterCtx {}\n89\tunsafe impl Sync for GkrInputScatterCtx {}\n90\t```\n91\t\n92\t### Change 2: New batched SCATTER kernel\n93\t\n94\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu` (append)\n95\t\n96\t```cuda\n97\t__global__ void batched_evaluate_interactions_scatter_kernel(\n98\t    const BlockCtx *__restrict__ d_block_ctxs,\n99\t    const GkrInputScatterCtx *__restrict__ d_air_ctxs\n100\t) {\n101\t    BlockCtx block_ctx = d_block_ctxs[blockIdx.x];\n102\t    GkrInputScatterCtx ctx = d_air_ctxs[block_ctx.air_idx];\n103\t\n104\t    // Per-block task distribution within this AIR\n105\t    uint32_t local_block = block_ctx.local_block_idx_x;\n106\t    uint32_t task_offset = local_block * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\n107\t    uint32_t task_stride = ctx.num_blocks * blockDim.x;\n108\t\n109\t    FpExt intermediates[10];  // Local array, same as SCATTER mode\n110\t    uint32_t intermediate_stride = 1;\n111\t\n112\t    // Same DAG evaluation loop as existing SCATTER kernel (gkr_input.cu lines 94-207)\n113\t    // using ctx.d_rules, ctx.d_used_nodes, ctx.d_pair_idxs, etc.\n114\t    // Guard: if (task_offset >= ctx.permutation_height) return;\n115\t    // ... (copy evaluation loop body from lines 94-207, replacing\n116\t    //      kernel arguments with ctx.field references)\n117\t}\n118\t```\n119\t\n120\tLauncher:\n121\t```cuda\n122\textern \"C\" int _batched_gkr_input_eval_scatter(\n123\t    const BlockCtx *d_block_ctxs,\n124\t    const GkrInputScatterCtx *d_air_ctxs,\n125\t    uint32_t num_blocks\n126\t) {\n127\t    if (num_blocks == 0) return 0;\n128\t    dim3 grid(num_blocks);\n129\t    dim3 block(256);\n130\t    batched_evaluate_interactions_scatter_kernel<<<grid, block>>>(\n131\t        d_block_ctxs, d_air_ctxs\n132\t    );\n133\t    return CHECK_KERNEL();\n134\t}\n135\t```\n136\t\n137\t### Change 3: Rust FFI + safe wrapper for batched scatter kernel\n138\t\n139\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n140\t\n141\tAdd extern declaration and safe wrapper:\n142\t```rust\n143\textern \"C\" {\n144\t    fn _batched_gkr_input_eval_scatter(\n145\t        block_ctxs: *const BlockCtx,\n146\t        air_ctxs: *const GkrInputScatterCtx,\n147\t        num_blocks: u32,\n148\t    ) -> i32;\n149\t}\n150\t\n151\tpub unsafe fn batched_gkr_input_eval_scatter(\n152\t    block_ctxs: &DeviceBuffer<BlockCtx>,\n153\t    air_ctxs: &DeviceBuffer<GkrInputScatterCtx>,\n154\t    num_blocks: u32,\n155\t) -> Result<(), CudaError> {\n156\t    check_error(_batched_gkr_input_eval_scatter(\n157\t        block_ctxs.as_ptr(),\n158\t        air_ctxs.as_ptr(),\n159\t        num_blocks,\n160\t    ))\n161\t}\n162\t```\n163\t\n164\t### Change 4: Restructure `log_gkr_input_evals` to separate SCATTER and GLOBAL AIRs\n165\t\n166\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`\n167\t\n168\tAfter building and sorting work_items (line 252), partition by mode:\n169\t\n170\t```rust\n171\t// Separate SCATTER and GLOBAL work items (preserving height-sorted order within each group)\n172\tlet mut scatter_indices: Vec<usize> = Vec::new();\n173\tlet mut global_indices: Vec<usize> = Vec::new();\n174\tfor (idx, w) in work_items.iter().enumerate() {\n175\t    if w.pk_air.other_data.interaction_rules.inner.buffer_size <= 10 {\n176\t        scatter_indices.push(idx);\n177\t    } else {\n178\t        global_indices.push(idx);\n179\t    }\n180\t}\n181\t```\n182\t\n183\tBuild SCATTER descriptor arrays (main thread, before spawning workers):\n184\t```rust\n185\t// Build BlockCtx and GkrInputScatterCtx for all SCATTER AIRs\n186\tlet mut block_ctxs: Vec<BlockCtx> = Vec::new();\n187\tlet mut air_ctxs: Vec<GkrInputScatterCtx> = Vec::new();\n188\tfor (air_local_idx, &work_idx) in scatter_indices.iter().enumerate() {\n189\t    let w = &work_items[work_idx];\n190\t    let height = w.air_ctx.height() as u32;\n191\t    let num_air_blocks = height.div_ceil(256);\n192\t\n193\t    for local_block in 0..num_air_blocks {\n194\t        block_ctxs.push(BlockCtx {\n195\t            local_block_idx_x: local_block,\n196\t            air_idx: air_local_idx as u32,\n197\t        });\n198\t    }\n199\t\n200\t    // Build per-AIR context (collecting pointers from existing data structures)\n201\t    air_ctxs.push(GkrInputScatterCtx { /* fields from work item */ });\n202\t}\n203\tlet d_block_ctxs = block_ctxs.to_device()?;\n204\tlet d_air_ctxs = air_ctxs.to_device()?;\n205\tlet total_scatter_blocks = block_ctxs.len() as u32;\n206\t```\n207\t\n208\tModify the multi-threaded section to only process GLOBAL AIRs:\n209\t```rust\n210\t// Adjust num_threads based on GLOBAL count (not total)\n211\tlet mut num_threads = if global_indices.len() >= 100 {\n212\t    NUM_GKR_INPUT_STREAMS.min(global_indices.len())\n213\t} else if global_indices.is_empty() {\n214\t    0\n215\t} else {\n216\t    1\n217\t};\n218\t// ... memory budget check on GLOBAL-only buffer sizes ...\n219\t```\n220\t\n221\t### Change 5: Launch SCATTER batch on background thread\n222\t\n223\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`\n224\t\n225\tInside the `std::thread::scope` block, add a background thread for SCATTER batch:\n226\t\n227\t```rust\n228\tstd::thread::scope(|s| {\n229\t    // Background thread: batched SCATTER evaluation\n230\t    let scatter_handle = if total_scatter_blocks > 0 {\n231\t        Some(s.spawn(move || -> Result<(), InteractionGpuError> {\n232\t            unsafe {\n233\t                batched_gkr_input_eval_scatter(\n234\t                    &d_block_ctxs, &d_air_ctxs, total_scatter_blocks\n235\t                )?;\n236\t            }\n237\t            // Lifting for SCATTER AIRs that need it\n238\t            for &work_idx in &scatter_indices {\n239\t                let w = &work_items[work_idx];\n240\t                let height = w.air_ctx.height();\n241\t                let lifted_height = max(height, 1 << w.l_skip);\n242\t                if height != lifted_height {\n243\t                    // Launch per-AIR lifting kernels on this thread's stream\n244\t                    // (sequential, after batch kernel completes)\n245\t                    // ... frac_vector_scalar_multiply_ext_fp + frac_matrix_vertically_repeat\n246\t                }\n247\t            }\n248\t            current_stream_sync().map_err(InteractionGpuError::from)?;\n249\t            Ok(())\n250\t        }))\n251\t    } else {\n252\t        None\n253\t    };\n254\t\n255\t    // Worker threads: GLOBAL-mode AIRs only\n256\t    let global_handles: Vec<_> = /* ... existing multi-stream dispatch using global_indices ... */;\n257\t\n258\t    // Join all\n259\t    if let Some(h) = scatter_handle { h.join().unwrap()?; }\n260\t    for h in global_handles { h.join().unwrap()?; }\n261\t    Ok::<_, InteractionGpuError>(())\n262\t})?;\n263\t```\n264\t\n265\t**Borrow checker**: `work_items`, `scatter_indices`, `d_block_ctxs`, `d_air_ctxs` are all borrowed/captured by the scatter thread. Since they're within `thread::scope`, the borrows are safe. `d_block_ctxs` and `d_air_ctxs` are `DeviceBuffer` values that are moved into the scatter thread closure.\n266\t\n267\t## Invariants\n268\t\n269\t1. **Correctness**: Every AIR is processed exactly once. SCATTER AIRs go through the batched kernel; GLOBAL AIRs go through the existing multi-stream path. Both write to the same `leaves` buffer at pre-computed non-overlapping per-AIR offsets.\n270\t\n271\t2. **Output equivalence**: The batched SCATTER kernel uses the same DAG evaluation logic as the existing `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<false>`, just with per-block descriptors instead of per-launch arguments.\n272\t\n273\t3. **Single-thread fallback**: At APC 0 (99 AIRs < 100 threshold), all AIRs are processed sequentially on the main thread (unchanged).\n274\t\n275\t4. **Memory safety**: `GkrInputScatterCtx` pointers reference device data that is valid for the lifetime of `log_gkr_input_evals`. No SCATTER intermediates buffer is needed (local array of 10 elements).\n276\t\n277\t5. **APC 0 no-regression**: Threshold check ensures single-threaded path is used at APC 0.\n278\t\n279\t6. **GLOBAL path unchanged**: GLOBAL-mode AIRs use the existing multi-stream processing with pre-allocated per-thread buffers.\n280\t\n281\t## Measurement Plan\n282\t\n283\tRun the standard benchmark:\n284\t```bash\n285\tcd /home/georg/powdr/results/pairing\n286\t/home/georg/powdr/target/release/powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics <path> --recursion\n287\t```\n288\t\n289\tKey metrics (APC 300):\n290\t- **LogUp GKR**: current ~534ms, expect 10-25ms improvement\n291\t- **STARK excl trace**: current ~1312ms, expect proportional improvement\n292\t- No regression in Round 0, MLE Rounds, Trace Commit, Openings\n293\t\n294\tKey metrics (APC 000): must not regress.\n295\t\n296\tRun each configuration at least twice.\n297\t\n298\t## Rollback Criteria\n299\t\n300\tRevert if ANY of:\n301\t- LogUp GKR at APC 300 improves by less than 10ms (median of 2+ runs)\n302\t- STARK excl trace at APC 300 regresses by more than 20ms\n303\t- Any APC 0 metric regresses by more than 30ms\n304\t- Proof verification fails\n305\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WVgYuHXQhJGV2tfoj6TCzi","session_id":"d4314f39-e91d-47fe-87bd-a8908ed81e1e","uuid":"03dc4af6-ebd8-4269-80d8-4c57122800f0","timestamp":"2026-04-14T09:15:35.051Z"}
