{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013C8znBTwjXDp2QrkstzFCk","type":"tool_result","content":"260\t### Change 6: Restructure `log_gkr_input_evals` orchestration\n261\t\n262\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`\n263\t\n264\tAfter sorting work_items (line 252), partition into SCATTER and GLOBAL groups. Build SCATTER descriptor arrays (Changes 2-3). Then in the thread::scope block:\n265\t\n266\t- If `work_items.len() < 100`: use existing single-threaded path for ALL AIRs (unchanged, no batching). This preserves the APC 0 fallback exactly.\n267\t- If `work_items.len() >= 100`:\n268\t  - Spawn background thread for SCATTER batch (if any SCATTER AIRs exist)\n269\t  - Spawn 8 worker threads for GLOBAL AIRs only (using contiguous chunks of height-sorted GLOBAL items, same existing pattern)\n270\t  - Join all threads\n271\t\n272\tThread count for GLOBAL workers: `min(NUM_GKR_INPUT_STREAMS, global_indices.len())`. Memory budget check uses only GLOBAL AIRs' max buffer sizes (SCATTER AIRs don't need `GkrThreadBuffers`).\n273\t\n274\t## Invariants\n275\t\n276\t1. **Correctness**: Every AIR processed exactly once. SCATTER → batched kernel, GLOBAL → multi-stream. Non-overlapping output regions in `leaves`.\n277\t\n278\t2. **Output equivalence**: Batched SCATTER kernel uses identical DAG evaluation logic as `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<false>`.\n279\t\n280\t3. **APC 0 fallback**: Guard `work_items.len() >= 100` ensures APC 0 (99 AIRs) uses the unchanged single-threaded path. No SCATTER batching at APC 0.\n281\t\n282\t4. **Lifting correctness**: Lifted SCATTER AIRs write to a shared `d_scatter_tmp` buffer (one at a time, sequentially on the background thread). Non-lifted SCATTER AIRs write directly to `leaves`. The tmp buffer is large enough for the biggest lifted SCATTER AIR.\n283\t\n284\t5. **Memory safety**: All descriptor pointers reference device data valid for the `log_gkr_input_evals` lifetime. SCATTER intermediates are local arrays (10 elements, no device buffer needed). The `d_scatter_tmp` buffer is allocated on the main thread and borrowed by the background thread within `thread::scope`.\n285\t\n286\t6. **GLOBAL path unchanged**: GLOBAL-mode processing is identical except it receives fewer work items.\n287\t\n288\t## Measurement Plan\n289\t\n290\tRun the standard benchmark:\n291\t```bash\n292\tcd /home/georg/powdr/results/pairing\n293\t/home/georg/powdr/target/release/powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics <path> --recursion\n294\t```\n295\t\n296\tKey metrics (APC 300):\n297\t- **LogUp GKR**: current ~534ms, expect 10-20ms improvement\n298\t- **STARK excl trace**: current ~1312ms, expect proportional improvement\n299\t- No regression in Round 0, MLE Rounds, Trace Commit, Openings"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019drUhnLnZVuh4yqgaLTUU7","session_id":"d4314f39-e91d-47fe-87bd-a8908ed81e1e","uuid":"a41ce8df-65ae-46e2-bbe1-fb2b44943b94","timestamp":"2026-04-14T09:22:40.522Z"}
