{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BUkuHAC3bsp7nGGFiPpFXC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Batch SCATTER-mode GKR Input Evaluation\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tReduce LogUp GKR input evaluation wall-clock time at APC 300 by batching SCATTER-mode AIR evaluations (buffer_size <= 10) into a single descriptor-array CUDA kernel per segment, launched on a dedicated background thread concurrent with the existing multi-stream GLOBAL-mode processing.\n6\t\n7\tLogUp GKR is 534ms (40.7% of STARK excl trace at APC 300). The GKR input eval sub-phase is ~302ms across 2 segments (~242ms seg0, ~62ms seg1). From nsight profiling: 486 GLOBAL-mode instances (464ms GPU time, median 760us) + 305 SCATTER-mode instances (63ms GPU time, median 111us). SCATTER AIRs each launch a tiny kernel with 4-16 blocks that underutilizes the 128 SMs.\n8\t\n9\t**Key mechanism**: Remove ~150 SCATTER AIRs per segment from the 8 multi-stream worker threads. Each thread processes ~20 GLOBAL-only AIRs instead of ~39 mixed AIRs. The SCATTER batch runs on a 9th background thread, hidden behind the GLOBAL processing. Each GLOBAL worker thread saves ~19 per-AIR overheads: CPU preparation (~25us), kernel launch (~10us), and between-kernel scheduling gap (~50us). Per-thread savings: ~1.6ms. The critical-path thread improves because its total serial work is shorter.\n10\t\n11\tAdditionally, the batched SCATTER kernel (one launch, ~1500 blocks) processes all SCATTER AIRs with optimal GPU block scheduling, vs the current approach where tiny 4-16 block kernels leave most SMs idle during each launch.\n12\t\n13\t**Performance risk**: The prior `gkr-input-round-robin` task (8ms, reverted) showed that scheduling improvements at this phase have limited impact because aggregate kernel execution time dominates. This plan targets a different mechanism (removing work from threads rather than rebalancing), but the per-thread savings (~1.6ms) are modest. The improvement is expected to be 10-20ms, close to the rollback threshold.\n14\t\n15\t## Current Code Path\n16\t\n17\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`\n18\t\n19\t1. **`log_gkr_input_evals()`** (line 215): Entry point.\n20\t   - Line 232-252: Build `Vec<GkrInputWorkItem>`, sort by descending height\n21\t   - Line 254-279: Compute max buffer sizes for pre-allocation\n22\t   - Line 282: Barrier sync\n23\t   - Line 285-289: Set num_threads (8 if >= 100 AIRs, else 1)\n24\t   - Line 291-303: Memory budget check (halve num_threads if pre-alloc > 2GB)\n25\t   - Line 306-321: Pre-allocate per-thread `GkrThreadBuffers`\n26\t   - Line 328-348: Multi-threaded processing: contiguous chunks, all AIR types mixed\n27\t\n28\t2. **`process_gkr_input_air()`** (line 112): Per-AIR processing.\n29\t   - Line 125-129: Build partition pointers from cached_mains + common_main\n30\t   - Line 141-148: Upload public_values to device via `copy_to`\n31\t   - Line 152-156: Upload partition_ptrs to device via `copy_to`\n32\t   - Line 158-160: `is_global = buffer_size > 10` — determines SCATTER vs GLOBAL mode\n33\t   - Line 173-187: Single FFI call: `logup_gkr_input_eval(is_global, ...)`\n34\t   - Line 189-208: Conditional lifting: if height != lifted_height, scale + repeat\n35\t\n36\t3. **CUDA kernel**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu`\n37\t   - Line 65-208: `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<GLOBAL>` template\n38\t   - SCATTER (GLOBAL=false, line 89-92): `FpExt intermediates[10]` — local array, max 10 nodes\n39\t   - GLOBAL (GLOBAL=true, line 85-87): `d_intermediates` global buffer, stride = task_stride\n40\t   - Line 17-63: `evaluate_dag_entry_gkr()` — switch on SourceInfo.type to load data\n41\t   - Line 94-207: Per-row loop: iterate d_used_nodes, evaluate DAG, write to d_fracs\n42\t   - Line 216-265: Launcher: `grid = kernel_launch_params(is_global ? TASK_SIZE : height, 256)`\n43\t\n44\t4. **FFI**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n45\t   - Line 278-292: extern declaration\n46\t   - Line 938-968: safe wrapper `logup_gkr_input_eval()`\n47\t\n48\t**Existing batched pattern reference**: `ZerocheckCtx` (line 48-58 of `cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`) + `BlockCtx` (line 17-22) used by `zerocheck_batch_mle_kernel` in `cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle.cu`.\n49\t\n50\t## Changes\n51\t\n52\t### Change 1: Define GkrInputScatterCtx descriptor struct\n53\t\n54\t**Files**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu` (CUDA) and `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` (Rust)\n55\t\n56\tCUDA side:\n57\t```cuda\n58\tstruct GkrInputScatterCtx {\n59\t    FracExt *d_fracs;               // Per-AIR output pointer (into leaves or tmp buffer)\n60\t    const Fp *d_preprocessed;       // Per-AIR preprocessed trace (or null ptr)\n61\t    const uint64_t *d_main;         // Per-AIR: pointer into concatenated partition-ptr array\n62\t    const Fp *d_public_values;      // Per-AIR: pointer into concatenated public-values array (or null)\n63\t    const FpExt *d_challenges;      // Shared challenge vector (same for all AIRs)\n64\t    const Rule *d_rules;            // Per-AIR: already on device in pk_air\n65\t    const size_t *d_used_nodes;     // Per-AIR: already on device in pk_air\n66\t    const uint32_t *d_pair_idxs;    // Per-AIR: already on device in pk_air\n67\t    size_t used_nodes_len;          // Per-AIR\n68\t    uint32_t permutation_height;    // Per-AIR trace height\n69\t    uint32_t num_blocks;            // Blocks assigned to this AIR\n70\t};\n71\t```\n72\t\n73\tRust side:\n74\t```rust\n75\t#[repr(C)]\n76\t#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]\n77\tpub struct GkrInputScatterCtx {\n78\t    pub d_fracs: *mut Frac<EF>,\n79\t    pub d_preprocessed: *const F,\n80\t    pub d_main: *const u64,\n81\t    pub d_public_values: *const F,\n82\t    pub d_challenges: *const EF,\n83\t    pub d_rules: *const std::ffi::c_void,\n84\t    pub d_used_nodes: *const usize,\n85\t    pub d_pair_idxs: *const u32,\n86\t    pub used_nodes_len: usize,\n87\t    pub permutation_height: u32,\n88\t    pub num_blocks: u32,\n89\t}\n90\tunsafe impl Send for GkrInputScatterCtx {}\n91\tunsafe impl Sync for GkrInputScatterCtx {}\n92\t```\n93\t\n94\t### Change 2: Concatenated H2D upload and descriptor construction (on background thread)\n95\t\n96\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`\n97\t\n98\t**Stream ordering**: All SCATTER H2D uploads, descriptor construction, and kernel launch happen on the **background thread's** CUDA stream (`cudaStreamPerThread`). This avoids cross-stream ordering issues — the background thread's stream serializes its own H2D uploads before the kernel launch automatically.\n99\t\n100\tThe background thread receives only the `scatter_indices` (computed on the main thread), plus shared references to `work_items` and `d_challenges`. It does all prep work internally:\n101\t\n102\t```rust\n103\t// Inside the background thread closure:\n104\t// Step 1: Concatenate host arrays for partition pointers and public values\n105\tlet mut all_partition_ptrs: Vec<u64> = Vec::new();\n106\tlet mut all_public_values: Vec<F> = Vec::new();\n107\tlet mut scatter_partition_offsets: Vec<usize> = Vec::new();\n108\tlet mut scatter_pv_offsets: Vec<usize> = Vec::new();\n109\t\n110\tfor &work_idx in &scatter_indices {\n111\t    let w = &work_items[work_idx];\n112\t    let air_ctx = w.air_ctx;\n113\t\n114\t    scatter_partition_offsets.push(all_partition_ptrs.len());\n115\t    for committed in &air_ctx.cached_mains {\n116\t        all_partition_ptrs.push(committed.trace.buffer().as_ptr() as u64);\n117\t    }\n118\t    all_partition_ptrs.push(air_ctx.common_main.buffer().as_ptr() as u64);\n119\t\n120\t    scatter_pv_offsets.push(all_public_values.len());\n121\t    all_public_values.extend_from_slice(&air_ctx.public_values);\n122\t}\n123\t\n124\t// 2 bulk H2D uploads (on this thread's stream)\n125\tlet d_all_partition_ptrs = all_partition_ptrs.to_device()?;\n126\tlet d_all_public_values = if all_public_values.is_empty() {\n127\t    DeviceBuffer::new()\n128\t} else {\n129\t    all_public_values.to_device()?\n130\t};\n131\t\n132\t// Step 2: Build BlockCtx and GkrInputScatterCtx arrays\n133\tlet mut block_ctxs: Vec<BlockCtx> = Vec::new();\n134\tlet mut air_ctxs: Vec<GkrInputScatterCtx> = Vec::new();\n135\t\n136\tfor (air_local_idx, &work_idx) in scatter_indices.iter().enumerate() {\n137\t    let w = &work_items[work_idx];\n138\t    let air_ctx = w.air_ctx;\n139\t    let pk_air = w.pk_air;\n140\t    let height = air_ctx.height() as u32;\n141\t    let num_air_blocks = height.div_ceil(256);\n142\t    let rules = &pk_air.other_data.interaction_rules;\n143\t\n144\t    // BlockCtx entries: one per block for this AIR\n145\t    for local_block in 0..num_air_blocks {\n146\t        block_ctxs.push(BlockCtx {\n147\t            local_block_idx_x: local_block,\n148\t            air_idx: air_local_idx as u32,\n149\t        });\n150\t    }\n151\t\n152\t    // Per-AIR descriptor\n153\t    let preprocessed_ptr = pk_air.preprocessed_data\n154\t        .as_ref()\n155\t        .map(|c| c.trace.buffer().as_ptr())\n156\t        .unwrap_or(std::ptr::null());\n157\t    let pv_ptr = if air_ctx.public_values.is_empty() {\n158\t        std::ptr::null()\n159\t    } else {\n160\t        unsafe { d_all_public_values.as_ptr().add(scatter_pv_offsets[air_local_idx]) }\n161\t    };\n162\t    let height_usize = air_ctx.height();\n163\t    let lifted_height = max(height_usize, 1 << w.l_skip);\n164\t    let fracs_ptr = if height_usize != lifted_height {\n165\t        d_scatter_tmp.as_mut_ptr()  // lifted AIR → write to tmp\n166\t    } else {\n167\t        w.leaves_ptr.0  // non-lifted → write directly to leaves\n168\t    };\n169\t\n170\t    air_ctxs.push(GkrInputScatterCtx {\n171\t        d_fracs: fracs_ptr,\n172\t        d_preprocessed: preprocessed_ptr,\n173\t        d_main: unsafe { d_all_partition_ptrs.as_ptr().add(scatter_partition_offsets[air_local_idx]) },\n174\t        d_public_values: pv_ptr,\n175\t        d_challenges: d_challenges_ref.as_ptr(),\n176\t        d_rules: rules.inner.d_rules.as_ptr() as *const _,\n177\t        d_used_nodes: rules.inner.d_used_nodes.as_ptr(),\n178\t        d_pair_idxs: rules.d_pair_idxs.as_ptr(),\n179\t        used_nodes_len: rules.inner.d_used_nodes.len(),\n180\t        permutation_height: height,\n181\t        num_blocks: num_air_blocks,\n182\t    });\n183\t}\n184\t\n185\tlet total_scatter_blocks = block_ctxs.len() as u32;\n186\tlet d_block_ctxs = block_ctxs.to_device()?;\n187\tlet d_air_ctxs = air_ctxs.to_device()?;\n188\t\n189\t// Step 3: Launch batched kernel (on this thread's stream, after uploads)\n190\tunsafe {\n191\t    batched_gkr_input_eval_scatter(&d_block_ctxs, &d_air_ctxs, total_scatter_blocks)?;\n192\t}\n193\t\n194\t// Step 4: Sequential lifting for SCATTER AIRs that need it\n195\t// (see Change 3)\n196\t```\n197\t\n198\tThis approach ensures all GPU work (H2D uploads → kernel launch → lifting) runs on the same CUDA stream, with correct ordering guaranteed by stream semantics.\n199\t\n200\t### Change 3: Handle lifting for SCATTER AIRs\n201\t\n202\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`\n203\t\n204\tSCATTER AIRs where `height != lifted_height` (height < 2^l_skip) need post-processing: scale by norm_factor and vertically repeat. Strategy:\n205\t\n206\t1. During descriptor construction, check if the AIR needs lifting.\n207\t2. For **non-lifted** SCATTER AIRs: `d_fracs` in the descriptor points directly to the AIR's slice in the `leaves` buffer.\n208\t3. For **lifted** SCATTER AIRs: `d_fracs` points to a shared tmp buffer. After the batched kernel completes, the background thread processes lifted AIRs sequentially — calling `frac_vector_scalar_multiply_ext_fp` + `frac_matrix_vertically_repeat` for each, reusing the same tmp buffer between AIRs.\n209\t\n210\tTmp buffer allocation:\n211\t```rust\n212\t// Compute max tmp size across lifted SCATTER AIRs\n213\tlet max_scatter_tmp = scatter_indices.iter()\n214\t    .filter_map(|&idx| {\n215\t        let w = &work_items[idx];\n216\t        let height = w.air_ctx.height();\n217\t        let lifted = max(height, 1 << w.l_skip);\n218\t        let n_int = w.pk_air.vk.symbolic_constraints.interactions.len();\n219\t        if height != lifted { Some(height * n_int) } else { None }\n220\t    })\n221\t    .max()\n222\t    .unwrap_or(0);\n223\t\n224\tlet d_scatter_tmp = if max_scatter_tmp > 0 {\n225\t    DeviceBuffer::<Frac<EF>>::with_capacity(max_scatter_tmp)\n226\t} else {\n227\t    DeviceBuffer::new()\n228\t};\n229\t```\n230\t\n231\tFor each lifted SCATTER AIR in the descriptor: set `d_fracs = d_scatter_tmp.as_mut_ptr()`. After the batched kernel completes on the background thread, process lifted AIRs sequentially:\n232\t\n233\t```rust\n234\t// On background thread, after batch kernel completes:\n235\tfor &work_idx in &scatter_indices {\n236\t    let w = &work_items[work_idx];\n237\t    let height = w.air_ctx.height();\n238\t    let lifted_height = max(height, 1 << w.l_skip);\n239\t    if height != lifted_height {\n240\t        let n_int = w.pk_air.vk.symbolic_constraints.interactions.len();\n241\t        let norm_factor = F::from_usize(lifted_height / height).inverse();\n242\t        unsafe {\n243\t            frac_vector_scalar_multiply_ext_fp(\n244\t                d_scatter_tmp.as_mut_ptr(), norm_factor, (height * n_int) as u32\n245\t            )?;\n246\t            frac_matrix_vertically_repeat(\n247\t                w.leaves_ptr.0, d_scatter_tmp.as_ptr(),\n248\t                n_int as u32, lifted_height as u32, height as u32\n249\t            )?;\n250\t        }\n251\t    }\n252\t}\n253\t```\n254\t\n255\t**Correctness**: Only one lifted AIR uses `d_scatter_tmp` at a time (sequential processing). Non-lifted AIRs write directly to leaves. The tmp buffer is reused between lifted AIRs (kernel outputs are consumed by the lifting kernels before the next lifted AIR starts).\n256\t\n257\t### Change 4: New batched SCATTER kernel\n258\t\n259\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.cu` (append)\n260\t\n261\t```cuda\n262\t__global__ void batched_evaluate_interactions_scatter_kernel(\n263\t    const BlockCtx *__restrict__ d_block_ctxs,\n264\t    const GkrInputScatterCtx *__restrict__ d_air_ctxs\n265\t) {\n266\t    BlockCtx block_ctx = d_block_ctxs[blockIdx.x];\n267\t    GkrInputScatterCtx ctx = d_air_ctxs[block_ctx.air_idx];\n268\t\n269\t    uint32_t local_block = block_ctx.local_block_idx_x;\n270\t    uint32_t task_offset = local_block * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;\n271\t    uint32_t task_stride = ctx.num_blocks * blockDim.x;\n272\t\n273\t    FpExt intermediates[10];\n274\t    uint32_t intermediate_stride = 1;\n275\t\n276\t    // Guard: boundary check\n277\t    if (task_offset >= ctx.permutation_height) return;\n278\t\n279\t    // DAG evaluation loop — same logic as gkr_input.cu lines 94-207\n280\t    // but reading from ctx.d_rules, ctx.d_used_nodes, ctx.d_pair_idxs,\n281\t    // ctx.d_preprocessed, ctx.d_main, ctx.d_public_values, ctx.d_challenges\n282\t    // and writing to ctx.d_fracs\n283\t    // num_rows_per_tile = 1 for SCATTER mode (height <= TASK_SIZE)\n284\t    // ...\n285\t}\n286\t\n287\textern \"C\" int _batched_gkr_input_eval_scatter(\n288\t    const BlockCtx *d_block_ctxs,\n289\t    const GkrInputScatterCtx *d_air_ctxs,\n290\t    uint32_t num_blocks\n291\t) {\n292\t    if (num_blocks == 0) return 0;\n293\t    dim3 grid(num_blocks);\n294\t    dim3 block(256);\n295\t    batched_evaluate_interactions_scatter_kernel<<<grid, block>>>(\n296\t        d_block_ctxs, d_air_ctxs\n297\t    );\n298\t    return CHECK_KERNEL();\n299\t}\n300\t```\n301\t\n302\t### Change 5: Rust FFI + safe wrapper\n303\t\n304\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n305\t\n306\t```rust\n307\textern \"C\" {\n308\t    fn _batched_gkr_input_eval_scatter(\n309\t        block_ctxs: *const BlockCtx,\n310\t        air_ctxs: *const GkrInputScatterCtx,\n311\t        num_blocks: u32,\n312\t    ) -> i32;\n313\t}\n314\t\n315\tpub unsafe fn batched_gkr_input_eval_scatter(\n316\t    block_ctxs: &DeviceBuffer<BlockCtx>,\n317\t    air_ctxs: &DeviceBuffer<GkrInputScatterCtx>,\n318\t    num_blocks: u32,\n319\t) -> Result<(), CudaError> {\n320\t    check_error(_batched_gkr_input_eval_scatter(\n321\t        block_ctxs.as_ptr(), air_ctxs.as_ptr(), num_blocks,\n322\t    ))\n323\t}\n324\t```\n325\t\n326\t**CUDA header include**: The batched kernel in `gkr_input.cu` uses `BlockCtx` which is defined in `eval_ctx.cuh` under namespace `logup_zerocheck_mle`. Add `#include \"eval_ctx.cuh\"` at the top of `gkr_input.cu` and use `using logup_zerocheck_mle::BlockCtx;` inside the kernel, or define a local `GkrBlockCtx` struct with the same layout.\n327\t\n328\t### Change 6: Restructure `log_gkr_input_evals` orchestration\n329\t\n330\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs`\n331\t\n332\tAfter sorting work_items (line 252), partition into SCATTER and GLOBAL groups. Then in the thread::scope block:\n333\t\n334\t- If `work_items.len() < 100`: use existing single-threaded path for ALL AIRs (unchanged, no batching). This preserves the APC 0 fallback exactly.\n335\t- If `work_items.len() >= 100`:\n336\t  - Compute SCATTER/GLOBAL indices on main thread (pure CPU, trivial)\n337\t  - Allocate `d_scatter_tmp` on main thread (single DeviceBuffer::with_capacity)\n338\t  - Spawn background thread for SCATTER batch — this thread does ALL SCATTER prep internally: concatenated H2D uploads, descriptor construction, kernel launch, lifting (Change 2 + Change 3). Only `scatter_indices`, `work_items`, `d_challenges`, and `d_scatter_tmp` are borrowed from the parent scope.\n339\t  - Spawn 8 worker threads for GLOBAL AIRs only (using contiguous chunks of height-sorted GLOBAL items, same existing pattern)\n340\t  - Join all threads\n341\t\n342\tThread count for GLOBAL workers: `min(NUM_GKR_INPUT_STREAMS, global_indices.len())`. Memory budget check uses only GLOBAL AIRs' max buffer sizes (SCATTER AIRs don't need `GkrThreadBuffers`).\n343\t\n344\t## Invariants\n345\t\n346\t1. **Correctness**: Every AIR processed exactly once. SCATTER → batched kernel, GLOBAL → multi-stream. Non-overlapping output regions in `leaves`.\n347\t\n348\t2. **Output equivalence**: Batched SCATTER kernel uses identical DAG evaluation logic as `evaluate_interactions_gkr_kernel<false>`.\n349\t\n350\t3. **APC 0 fallback**: Guard `work_items.len() >= 100` ensures APC 0 (99 AIRs) uses the unchanged single-threaded path. No SCATTER batching at APC 0.\n351\t\n352\t4. **Lifting correctness**: Lifted SCATTER AIRs write to a shared `d_scatter_tmp` buffer (one at a time, sequentially on the background thread). Non-lifted SCATTER AIRs write directly to `leaves`. The tmp buffer is large enough for the biggest lifted SCATTER AIR.\n353\t\n354\t5. **Memory safety**: All descriptor pointers reference device data valid for the `log_gkr_input_evals` lifetime. SCATTER intermediates are local arrays (10 elements, no device buffer needed). The `d_scatter_tmp` buffer is allocated on the main thread and borrowed by the background thread within `thread::scope`.\n355\t\n356\t6. **GLOBAL path unchanged**: GLOBAL-mode processing is identical except it receives fewer work items.\n357\t\n358\t## Measurement Plan\n359\t\n360\tRun the standard benchmark:\n361\t```bash\n362\tcd /home/georg/powdr/results/pairing\n363\t/home/georg/powdr/target/release/powdr_openvm_riscv prove --artifact apc300.cbor --input 0 --metrics <path> --recursion\n364\t```\n365\t\n366\tKey metrics (APC 300):\n367\t- **LogUp GKR**: current ~534ms, expect 10-20ms improvement\n368\t- **STARK excl trace**: current ~1312ms, expect proportional improvement\n369\t- No regression in Round 0, MLE Rounds, Trace Commit, Openings\n370\t\n371\tKey metrics (APC 000): must not regress (single-threaded fallback unchanged).\n372\t\n373\tRun each configuration at least twice.\n374\t\n375\t## Rollback